# AN ARCH LINUX MICROVM RUNNING THE FULL GNOME STACK: GDM, THEN GNOME SHELL ON WAYLAND.
#
# THE DISPLAY MANAGER IS THE POINT. A bare `gnome-shell`, or a `gnome-session` launched outside a
# display manager, is NOT a full session: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome answers
#
#	Non-compatible display server, exposing settings only.
#
# and never provides ScreenCast. GDM starts its greeter, autologins vmuser, and registers
# org.gnome.Shell with the session manager - which is the condition the portal needs. MEASURED on
# this image: GDM comes up, autologin runs, and the shell paints the desktop.
#
# THE DISPLAY DEVICE IS virtio-gpu OVER PCIe. vkms has no render node (its driver_features leaves
# out DRIVER_RENDER) and vgem's render node has no output, so Mutter answered "No GPUs found" on
# both. MEASURED with `-M microvm,pcie=on` and `virtio-gpu-pci`:
#
#	[drm] Initialized virtio_gpu 0.1.0 for 0000:00:01.0 on minor 0
#	/sys/class/drm: card0 card0-Virtual-1 renderD128
#
# - one device with both a KMS output and a render node, which is what Mutter requires.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS QEMU'S OWN SCREENDUMP, NOT EASYSTREAM, AND THAT IS MEASURED RATHER THAN CHOSEN.
# The portal now EXPOSES ScreenCast on this backend, but `Start` answers
#
#	SelectDevices has NO restore token ... Start will ask for consent
#	no Response for /org/freedesktop/portal/desktop/request/1_84/est1
#
# - a consent dialog nobody can click on a headless boot, the same wall KWin has. GNOME's
# org.gnome.Shell.Screenshot is gated by an allowlist that only the portal backend holds, so
# neither shortcut works. What DOES work is the scanout itself: virtio-gpu drives a real
# framebuffer, so `see:` photographs the desktop the shell actually drew.

walkthrough "gnome microvm - the full GDM + gnome-shell stack on virtio-gpu"
resolution 1024x768
recording_resolution 1024x768
step "needs arch-vmlinuz arch-initramfs arch.qcow2"
  needs [arch-vmlinuz, arch-initramfs, arch.qcow2]

step "disk arch.qcow2"
  disk arch.qcow2

step "boot as a microvm from kernel \"arch-vmlinuz\" and initramfs \"arch-initramfs\" with \"console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4\" with a desktop with memory 1536, waiting up to 240s"
  boot
    machine "microvm,accel=kvm,acpi=on,pic=on,rtc=on,pcie=on,graphics=off"
    args [["-m", "1536"], ["-chardev", "socket,id=qga0,path={{work}}/qga.sock,server=on,wait=off"], ["-device", "isa-serial,chardev=qga0"], ["-device", "virtio-gpu-pci,xres=1024,yres=768"], ["-audiodev", "none,id=snd0"], ["-device", "ich9-intel-hda"], ["-device", "hda-duplex,audiodev=snd0"], ["-drive", "file={{disk}},if=none,format=qcow2,id=target{{discard}}"], ["-device", "virtio-blk-device,drive=target"], ["-netdev", "tap,id=net0,ifname=qemutap0,script=no,downscript=no"], ["-device", "virtio-net-device,netdev=net0,mac=52:54:00:56:4d:01"]]
    timeout 240
# THE KERNEL FOUND THE DISK AND USERSPACE STARTED.
step "the console will say \"login\""
  until login
  from console
  timeout 180

# GDM IS THE DISPLAY MANAGER, and it says so by starting under its own name.
step "the console will say \"GNOME Display Manager\""
  until "GNOME Display Manager"
  from console
  timeout 180

# AND THE CAPTURE UNIT FOUND GDM'S SOCKET. This is the line that proves a session (not just a
# greeter) exists: the unit only prints it after wayland-0 appeared in vmuser's runtime dir.
step "the console will say \"gdm-capture: socket=\""
  until "gdm-capture: socket="
  from console
  timeout 180

# GIVE THE SHELL TIME TO PAINT ITS FIRST FRAME AND THE AUTOLOGIN TO SETTLE.
step "wait 25s"
  settle 25

# THE PIXELS. A GDM that started with no GPU, or a shell that never got a session, leaves a
# black or uniform frame and fails this check. MEASURED on this image: the full desktop,
# wallpaper and top bar, at 1024x768.
step "read the whole screen as \"screen\""
  read
    name screen

# TWO QUESTIONS ABOUT ONE FRAME, BECAUSE "NOT BLACK" HAS TWO FAILURE SHAPES. A machine with no
# GPU records a uniformly BLACK frame; a shell that started but never painted a desktop records a
# uniformly COLOURED one. MEASURED on this image: mean 59 with a mean deviation of 21, against
# 0.0 and 0.03 for a dead frame.
step "the screen is not black"
  check
    source screen
    mode mean_between
    name gnome_is_not_black
    range [1, 255]
    rect [0, 0, 1024, 768]
    rect_at [1024, 768]

step "the screen is not one flat colour"
  check
    source screen
    mode spread_between
    name gnome_has_content
    range [1, 128]
    rect [0, 0, 1024, 768]
    rect_at [1024, 768]

step "stop the machine by killing it, waiting up to 60s"
  stop kill
  timeout 60
